WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.900
Having a food allergy can make for a

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.320
cautious existence -- carefully reading food labels,

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.440
being constantly aware of your surroundings

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.540
and carrying an Epi-pen can all

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.480
take their toll on a family’s well-being.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.740
And the problem isn’t getting any better --

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.680
the rate of food allergies has been rising rapidly,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.870
with peanuts being a prime example.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.540
The main strategy for those with a peanut allergy

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.380
is simple -- just stay away from peanuts.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.200
But that’s easier said than done.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.120
Peanuts appear in many foods

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.400
and totally avoiding the legume is nerve wracking.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.800
So researchers have turned to

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.480
the peanut itself for a solution.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.500
In the mid-2000s, researchers began administering

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.780
microdoses of peanuts to children with peanut allergies

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.760
in an attempt to disrupt the process

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.300
and desensitize the immune system.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.340
This treatment, dubbed “peanut immunotherapy,”

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.000
exposes children to very small but increasing

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.660
doses of peanut product, sometimes starting

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.280
with less than a 1/1000th of a peanut.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.100
Once inside the body, peanut proteins trigger

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.660
a cascade of immune activity.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.800
In tissues like the gut, the skin,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.380
and the respiratory system,  the antibody

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.760
called immunoglobulin E, or IgE,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.880
binds to white blood cells called mast cells.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.740
The food proteins get noticed by IgE,

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.220
which activates the mast cells.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.900
This leads to reactions throughout the body, from

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.080
hives on the skin, to stomach pain and throat swelling.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.200
Clinical trials of oral immunotherapy in food allergies

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.580
have shown some promising results.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:42.240
In many studies, after eating slowly increasing

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.060
quantities of the food for 6 to 12 months,

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.120
around 70% to 80% of patients

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.520
could handle higher doses than before.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.880
In one company-sponsored clinical trial,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.180
a peanut immunotherapy study of almost 500 children

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.880
and teens put the subjects on a regimen stepping

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.640
up through 11 dose levels over several months.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.580
About 20% on treatment dropped out of the study

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.740
for various reasons, including side effects.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:11.620
After about a year of treatment, 96% of those

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.620
who completed the treatment could consume

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.540
about one peanut with only mild symptoms;

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:21.040
84% could tolerate two; and 63% could tolerate

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.330
at least three peanuts.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.560
The company developing this capsule treatment,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.960
and a second that’s created a skin patch,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.100
are hoping to have their peanut immunotherapy

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.640
products on the market as soon as next year.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.060
The therapy is not without downsides --

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.820
in the case of oral immunotherapy, even children

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.720
who follow the treatment precisely

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.300
may experience allergic reactions.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.560
A stomach virus, physical activity

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.300
or even a hot shower can provoke allergic reactions

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.400
after taking a treatment dose -- and sometimes the

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.980
treatment can trigger a reaction

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.300
for no apparent reason at all.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.160
Still, despite the uncertainty, some families

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.500
with children who have food allergies welcome

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.360
the respite from everyday anxiety

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.740
that comes from avoiding hard-to-avoid foods.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.840
The new treatments aren’t cures, but with even more

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.160
food allergy therapies in the pipeline,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.740
there’s hope that families dealing with food allergies

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.800
will eventually be able to breathe a bit easier.

